  "title": "S2 \u00b7 Favourite\u2013longshot bias by surface and price",
  "hypothesis": {
    "statement": "Expected value declines as the price lengthens: on every surface the shortest bucket has a higher ROI than the longest, and no bucket's ROI interval lies entirely above zero.",
    "rationale": "Bettors overpay for longshots, so books can shade them harder; favourites are closer to fairly priced, though still net of the margin.",
